:: Carter Connor Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
As you get off the bus, ready for another long and boring day of school, you look up to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> standing by the entrance, looking nervously at his hands. Once he sees you, he smiles and hurries over, <span style="Color: Yellow">still looking very unsure but confident in what he wants to say.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>. Got a second?”</span> You nod and the two of you walk a few feet away, out of ear shot from anyone else as they all file into the school. <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                },
            },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Uniform",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 1,
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, I wanted to ask you something. You don’t have to say yes, it’s just…”</span> He pauses, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I wanted to go visit <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> – well – his grave. I’ve never actually been there before, outside of his funeral, but I don’t really remember that, and I’m… scared to go by myself and I can’t ask my family to take me so… would you come with me? Right now. We’ll be late for school and might get in trouble, I know, but… I… want us both to meet <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>, the real <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. You don’t have to, but-”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You stop <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s rambling right there, telling him you’ll go with him. How could you say no?</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Really?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> looks up happily, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thank you! Really! I promise I’ll tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Headmaster Alistair</span> or whoever that it was my fault we’re late, so you don’t get in trouble. I just… I need to see him. Talking to you about it… it made it feel more real than ever, that he’s gone. Mom… hasn’t mentioned him since that night. I guess, maybe if I see it, it’ll all make sense to me. I don’t know, it’s silly but-”</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">You take <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> by the hand, telling him to lead the way. He smiles, nodding as the two of you walk away from the school into town.</span> <br>
